"[2511.09516] MAP-VLA: Memory-Augmented Prompting for Vision-Language-Action Model in Robotic Manipulation (https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.09516)\nciteturn5914view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.09516\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 161\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Computer Science > Robotics\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 12 Nov 2025]\nL9: # Title:MAP-VLA: Memory-Augmented Prompting for Vision-Language-Action Model in Robotic Manipulation\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite5†Runhao Li , cite6†Wenkai Guo , cite7†Zhenyu Wu , cite8†Changyuan Wang , cite9†Haoyuan Deng , cite10†Zhenyu Weng , cite11†Yap-Peng Tan , cite12†Ziwei Wang L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled MAP-VLA: Memory-Augmented Prompting for Vision-Language-Action Model in Robotic Manipulation, by Runhao Li and 7 other authors\nL14: \nL15: cite13†View PDF cite14†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract:Pre-trained Vision-Language-Action (VLA) models have achieved remarkable success in improving robustness and generalization for end-to-end robotic manipulation. However, these models struggle with long-horizon tasks due to their lack of memory and reliance solely on immediate sensory inputs.\nL17: To address this limitation, we propose Memory-Augmented Prompting for Vision-Language-Action model (MAP-VLA), a novel framework that empowers pre-trained VLA models with demonstration-derived memory prompts to augment action generation for long-horizon robotic manipulation tasks. To achieve this, MAP-VLA first constructs a memory library from historical demonstrations, where each memory unit captures information about a specific stage of a task.\nL18: These memory units are implemented as learnable soft prompts optimized through prompt tuning. Then, during real-time task execution, MAP-VLA retrieves relevant memory through trajectory similarity matching and dynamically integrates it into the VLA model for augmented action generation. Importantly, this prompt tuning and retrieval augmentation approach operates as a plug-and-play module for a frozen VLA model, offering a lightweight and flexible solution to improve task performance.\nL19: Experimental results show that MAP-VLA delivers up to 7.0% absolute performance gains in the simulation benchmark and 25.0% on real robot evaluations for long-horizon tasks, surpassing the current state-of-the-art methods.\nL20: Subjects:  | Robotics (cs.RO); Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (cs.CV)\nL21: Cite as:  | cite15†arXiv:2511.09516 [cs.RO]\nL22:    | (or cite16†arXiv:2511.09516v1 [cs.RO] for this version)\nL23:    | cite17†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2511.09516†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL24: ## Submission history\nL25: \nL26: From: Runhao Li [cite18†view email ]\nL27: [v1] Wed, 12 Nov 2025 17:56:13 UTC (2,331 KB)\nL28: \nL29: Full-text links:\nL30: \nL31: ## Access Paper:\nL32: \nL33: View a PDF of the paper titled MAP-VLA: Memory-Augmented Prompting for Vision-Language-Action Model in Robotic Manipulation, by Runhao Li and 7 other authors\nL34: \nL35:   * cite13†View PDF L36:   * cite14†HTML (experimental) L37:   * cite19†TeX Source L38: \nL39: cite20†view license L40: ### Current browse context:\nL41: \nL42: cs.RO\nL43: \nL44: cite21†< prev |   cite22†next > L45: \nL46: cite23†new | cite24†recent | cite25†2025-11 L47: \nL48: Change to browse by:\nL49: \nL50: cite26†cs L51: cite27†cs.CV L52: \nL53: ### References & Citations\nL54: \nL55:   * cite28†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu L56:   * cite29†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com L57:   * cite30†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org L58: \nL59: [Button: export BibTeX citation] Loading...\nL